  CL8NK Entry: dual-named_numerals
  Dual-named numerals - Let a numeral be a pair (name, shape), where the name is N and the shape is the two-point
  space Spec(Z/N) = {p, q}. Reading off the factors is evaluation at the points, the way you read a coordinate off a
  vector. Under CRT the numerals native form is Z/p × Z/q, and “N” is just the label on its quotient. Nothing is
  searched, because the numeral never exists without its legs
  Reference: CLINK L8 (Organism) — ⟨𐑦⋅𐑸⋅𐑾⋅𐑹⋅𐑐⋅𐑧⋅𐑲⋅𐑵⋅⊙⋅𐑫⋅𐑳⋅𐑟⟩ (from catalog)
  Catalog-native — no hardcoded systems
